==================================================
DAILY QA REPORT - BUG COUNT RULE CONFIGURATION
==================================================
Source of truth for: Total Bugs, P0, P1, Bugs With Dev, Bugs With QA, Bugs With Product (Approval/Discussion), Closed Bugs.
Referenced by: core/report_formatter.py
==================================================

GLOBAL FILTER CONDITIONS (APPLIES TO ALL COUNTS)
--------------------------------------------------
• Only include Issue Type = "Bug"
• Bug must be linked to a Main JIRA ID (parent story / task)
• Resolution must NOT be:
    - "Not a Bug"
    - "Duplicate"
• Exclude standalone/unlinked bugs
• Exclude cancelled or rejected tickets
• Always calculate dynamically from filtered JIRA data
• If no valid bugs exist, show count as 0


==================================================
SECTION 1: TOTAL BUG COUNT RULES
==================================================

"Total Bugs" must include:
• All valid bugs matching Global Filter Conditions
• Regardless of status (Dev / QA / Released)

Output format:
Total Bugs: <count>


==================================================
SECTION 2: P0 BUG COUNT RULES
==================================================

"P0" must include:
• All valid bugs matching Global Filter Conditions
• Issue Type / Priority = "P0"

Output format:
P0: <count>


==================================================
SECTION 3: P1 BUG COUNT RULES
==================================================

"P1" must include:
• All valid bugs matching Global Filter Conditions
• Issue Type / Priority = "P1"

Output format:
P1: <count>


==================================================
SECTION 4: BUGS WITH DEV COUNT RULES
==================================================

"Bugs With Dev" must include valid bugs where
Status is one of:

• "Open"
• "Tech Feasibility"
• "Ready For Development"
• "Development IP"
• "Development Review"
• "Bug Fixing IP"

Include reopened bugs if current status matches above.

Exclude:
• QA statuses
• Released status

Output format:
Bugs With Dev: <count>


==================================================
SECTION 5: BUGS WITH QA COUNT RULES
==================================================

"Bugs With QA" must include valid bugs where
Status is one of:

• "Ready for QA"
• "QA In Progress"
• "QA Review"
• "Ready For SIT"
• "SIT In Progress"
• "Ready To Release"

Include reopened bugs if current status matches above.

Exclude:
• Dev statuses
• Released status

Output format:
Bugs With QA: <count>


==================================================
SECTION 5a: BUGS WITH PRODUCT (APPROVAL/DISCUSSION) COUNT RULES
==================================================

"Bugs With Product (Approval/Discussion)" must include valid bugs where
Status is one of:

• "Ready for UAT"
• "Product UAT IP"

Include:
• Linked bugs awaiting product approval or in UAT discussion

Output format:
Bugs With Product (Approval/Discussion): <count>


==================================================
SECTION 6: CLOSED BUGS COUNT RULES
==================================================

"Closed Bugs" must include valid bugs where:

• Status = "Released"

Include:
• Successfully deployed production bugs

Exclude:
• Dev statuses
• QA statuses
• 'Not a Bug' and 'Duplicate' in Resolution

Output format:
Closed Bugs: <count>

==================================================
SECTION 7: Preprod Status
==================================================

Definition:
"Preprod Status" should show tickets that have moved into
Pre-Production stages.

1. If Status = Released, Beta Deployed, or Deployment Completed:
   Preprod Status = "Completed"

2. Else, if Status in Ready for SIT, SIT In Progress, Ready For Release:
   Preprod Status = "In-progress"

3. Otherwise: Preprod Status = "Pending"

==================================================
SECTION 8: UAT Status
==================================================

Definition:
"UAT Status" should show tickets that have moved into
User Acceptance Testing stages.

1. If Status = Released, Beta Deployed, or Deployment Completed:
   UAT Status = "Completed"

2. Else, if Preprod Status = In-progress (Ready for SIT, SIT In Progress, Ready For Release):
   UAT Status = "Completed"

3. Else, if Status in Ready for UAT, UAT In Progress, Product UAT IP:
   UAT Status = "In-UAT"

4. Otherwise: UAT Status = "Pending"


==================================================
SECTION 9: ENVIRONMENT ISSUE RULES
==================================================

Definition:
"Environment Issue" value must always reflect
the TOTAL number of LED tickets attached to JIRA.

1. Value Calculation:
   - Count ALL LED tickets linked to JIRA
     (regardless of status).

2. Open LED Handling:
   - Identify LEDs where Status = "Open".

3. Output Rules:

A) If Total LED = 0:
   Display:

   Environment Issues: 0
   No LED tickets linked to JIRA

B) If Total LED > 0 AND Open LED > 0:
   Display:

   Environment Issues: <Total LED Count>

   <Open LED Count> LED(s) in Open status:

   • <LED-ID> – <LED Summary> (Assignee: <Name>)

   • <LED-ID> – <LED Summary> (Assignee: <Name>)

C) If Total LED > 0 AND Open LED = 0:
   Display:

   Environment Issues: <Total LED Count>
   No LED tickets are currently in Open status


==================================================
SECTION 10: INTERNAL PEDS RULES
==================================================

Definition:
"Internal PEDS" count = number of linked issues with Issue Type
"PEDS Internal" or "Internal PEDS".

1. Value Calculation:
   - Count linked issues where issuetype = "PEDS Internal" or "Internal PEDS"

2. Output format:
   Internal PEDS: <count>


==================================================
END OF FILE
